xnu 0283: the sweep is a horizontal drag, and nothing else unless asked

`0280` made the synthetic finger horizontal and `0283` then put three seconds of
bottom-edge swipe up in front of it, so that an unattended boot could leave the
lock screen. On a home screen that gesture opens the app switcher, and the jump
from the bottom edge to the middle of the panel is read as a swipe: ring250
launched Spotlight that way, and a horizontal drag inside Spotlight draws
nothing, so the sweep measured an empty screen for two minutes.

The horizontal drag is the sweep again. The unlock prologue is still there for a
boot that cannot get out of the lock screen, behind `mondriandragunlock=1`; it is
off by default, and the phase clock of the pan does not move when it is on.

